  the daily school schedule or school  being in session i would say that the  largest threat to the industry has  become amazon the biggest thing that  happened during the pandemic when the  school buses were shut down is delivery  services boomed many of our potential  applicants went there instead so the  school bus industry could be recession  proof but it's not pandemic proof  whereas delivery services have proven  they're not only pandemic proof they're  pandemic booming the shortage is so  severe that in some states the national  guard was activated to fill the gaps  they're not sustainable solutions the  national guard's there to protect us  they're not there to be cdl school bus  drivers so it's a little bit different  for them this is a whole new area for  them where you don't have professional  experienced drivers on the road like  every other industry school bus  operators are increasing pay to attract  job seekers but it's complicated because  taxpayers often end up getting the final  say so here's the issue obviously you  want to give good raises you want to  give competitive benefits you want to  have a competitive pay scale but the  problem is is you're a business and you  have to pass that on to the school  district and then that becomes a vicious  cycle of fighting of who's responsible  for what and rebidding so i'm nervous  about inflation i'm nervous about the  supply chain and the demand  and uh  i don't know what gets done to mitigate  that so corey has to be creative and  pull the levers that are available to  him sure so we're offering sign-on  bonuses that this industry has never  seen we're offering  paint  but give me an idea between 2 500 and 3  and we're offering paid training uh  we're offering the training class to get  on the road immediately on the vans and  then go go to type c if you can only  work the pm we'll take you fine we'll  take whatever we could get you only want  to do three hours at four o'clock at  night we'll put you on